course: dictionary
lesson: 5597
title: Lidar: how machines see with light
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lidar is a way of measuring distance using light. It sends out quick flashes of laser light, then times how long each flash takes to bounce back. Light travels very fast, so that timing tells the machine how far away things are.
explain: Lidar can also mean the machine, or sensor, that does this. «A self-driving car uses cameras, radar and lidar to scan around it.» Here lidar is a sensor on the car, helping it see the road and the things on it.
explain: Think of a bat. It finds things by listening for echoes of sound. Lidar works in a similar way, but it uses light instead of sound. Use the clues around the word: «a spinning laser that times how long its light takes to bounce back» tells you what lidar does.
fact: Lidar means a way of measuring distance using laser light.
fact: Lidar can build a 3D picture, such as «a 3D picture of a street».
fact: Lidar is used to map forests, find hidden ruins under trees, and measure sea ice.
fact: Lidar helps robots and driverless cars avoid things.
fact: Lidar usually has no plural, but we can say «lidar scanners» for more than one machine.
exercise: «A spinning laser times how long its light takes to bounce back.» What does lidar do? | *It measures distance using light | It grows plants in the dark | It plays music through speakers | It makes loud echoes of sound
exercise: «Lidar helped scientists find old ruins hidden under the trees.» What did lidar help them find? | *Hidden ruins under trees | A lost football | The temperature of the sea water only | A new kind of bread
exercise: Bats find things by the echo of sound. What does lidar use instead? | Touch | Sound | Smell | *Light
test: Lidar works most like which animal's way of finding things? | Dog finding things by smell | *Bat finding things by echo | Snake sensing heat | Owl flying silently at night
test: In «a driverless car uses lidar to scan around it», what is lidar? | A bird that flies over roads | A road sign | *A sensor that scans around the car | A type of car
exam: Explain in your own words what lidar is, using the idea of light bouncing back. | *Lidar is a way to measure distance by timing laser light that bounces back from things | Lidar is a kind of bread eaten at breakfast | Lidar is a loud sound that bats make to find food | Lidar is a type of cloud that forms over hills
